  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Since force on a point charge by magnetic field is always perpendicular to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>v</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mover><mi>F</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi><mfenced><mrow><mover><mi>v</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>&#215;</mo><mover><mi>B</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math> Work by magnetic force on the point charge is zero.</p>",
